WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.740
- Some of the ways that
Ultima was quite unique

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.180
back in the 1980s was that you would start

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.660
through creating a character.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.940
Your character would even
have attributes like strength

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.110
and dexterity and stamina.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.160
Whatever it might be.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.770
It had the characters and the story.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.200
It had places where once
you had gone out on a battle

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.670
and fought that you can return to.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.430
A city or a town where you
could replenish your supplies,

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:26.320
rest up, heal up.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.690
Those sort of things.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.940
And so I sort of saw it as a world.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.633
A living, breathing fantasy
universe to play as a player.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.410
- [Narrator] In an industry

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.850
that had always assigned
players a character to play,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.870
a game like Ultima
allowed you to build one.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.520
It created an open world where
you could then venture forth

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.840
on epic quests and equip different weapons

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.203
and armor to aid you on your adventure.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.040
- With Ultima, in a very real way,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.380
I was finally beginning
to flex a little bit

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.320
of those game master roots.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.500
(suspenseful music)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.790
You're now being involved in a narrative

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.470
where I have laid out the
fundamentals of the narrative

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.066
but a lot of the details are
filled in by you the player.

00:01:13.066 --> 00:01:16.066
(suspenseful music)

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.200
- [Narrator] To be brutally honest,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.763
the game hasn't aged gracefully.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:29.080
But without this, you wouldn't have these.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.830
(dramatic music)

00:01:37.452 --> 00:01:39.100
In a short period of time,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.600
creators like Richard and
Roberta had taken computer games

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.160
from simple text on
screen to crude graphics,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.733
to character creation.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.210
The genre was evolving.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.000
Trying to perfect itself
within the limits of technology

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.523
and building upon each innovation.

